---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro"
import DocSection from "../../components/DocSection.astro"

const CONTACT_EMAIL = "me@maxlibin.com"
const EFFECTIVE_DATE = "24 September 2026"
---

<Base
  title="ZhouYi Master AI — Privacy Policy"
  description="What ZhouYi Master AI keeps on your iPhone, what it sends to Yi Master, and who processes it. No accounts, no ads, no trackers."
  pathname="/zhouyi-master-ai/privacy/"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", item: "/" },
    { name: "ZhouYi Master AI", item: "/zhouyi-master-ai/" },
    { name: "Privacy Policy", item: "/zhouyi-master-ai/privacy/" },
  ]}
>
  <article class="mt-8 mb-16 px-4 md:px-0 max-w-3xl">
    <div class="mb-3 text-sm">
      <a href="/zhouyi-master-ai/" class="text-fg hover:underline">
        ← ZhouYi Master AI
      </a>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-fg mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-faint mb-10">Effective {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

    <DocSection title="The short version">
      <p>
        ZhouYi Master AI is a Yijing (I Ching) reflection app for iPhone. We
        collect as little as we can and we don't sell anything.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>No account, no sign-up, no email required to use the app.</li>
        <li>
          No advertising SDKs, no analytics SDKs, no third-party trackers in the
          app.
        </li>
        <li>
          Your readings, journal, conversations, and profile stay on your
          device.
        </li>
        <li>
          When you talk with Yi Master, your message and the context it needs
          are sent to our server only to write the reply.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Who runs the app">
      <p>
        ZhouYi Master AI ("we", "us", "the app") is an independent product built
        and operated by Max Li Bin (Singapore). Contact:{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="text-fg hover:underline">
          {CONTACT_EMAIL}
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="What stays on your device">
      <p>The following never leaves your iPhone:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Your coin casts, readings, and journal.</li>
        <li>Your saved conversations with Yi Master.</li>
        <li>
          Your profile, including birth date and gender, which are never sent
          anywhere.
        </li>
        <li>
          Motion sensor readings used to toss the coins, which are processed on
          the device and not stored.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These are stored using Apple's standard on-device storage. They are
        included in your iCloud device backup only if you have iCloud backup
        enabled in iOS. Deleting the app removes them.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="What is sent when you talk with Yi Master">
      <p>
        When you send a message to Yi Master, the app sends the following to our
        backend (a Cloudflare Worker we operate) so it can write a reply:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Your message and the recent turns of that conversation.</li>
        <li>A reading you chose to attach, if any.</li>
        <li>
          The profile fields you filled in: name, situation, goals, and
          concerns.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Our backend passes this to DeepSeek's API to generate the reply and
        streams it back to you. We do not store your messages on our server.
        DeepSeek processes the request under its own privacy policy and may
        process it outside your country, including in the People's Republic of
        China.
      </p>
      <p>
        If our server cannot be reached and your iPhone supports Apple
        Intelligence, the reply is written by Apple's on-device model instead,
        and nothing is sent.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Install identifier and credits">
      <p>
        The app creates a random identifier for this installation and keeps it
        in your iPhone's Keychain. Our server uses it to keep your Yi Master
        balance: how many replies you have used, their token counts and cost,
        and which subscription, if any, this installation is linked to. It is
        not linked to your name, email, or Apple Account.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Subscriptions">
      <p>
        Payments are handled entirely by Apple. When you subscribe or restore
        purchases, the app sends Apple's signed transaction record (transaction
        identifiers, product, renewal date, and whether it is a test purchase)
        to our server, which checks Apple's signature and refills your monthly
        replies. We never see your payment details, full name, or Apple Account.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="IP address and logs">
      <p>
        Your IP address is used to enforce a daily request limit. It is kept
        only in a counter that expires at the end of the day (UTC).
      </p>
      <p>
        Our server keeps short-lived operational logs (for example request
        events and error messages) so we can keep the service running. These
        logs do not contain your messages and are not used for advertising or
        sold to anyone.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Analytics and tracking">
      <p>
        We do not embed advertising SDKs, analytics SDKs, or third-party
        trackers in the app. We do not use the IDFA. We do not build a profile
        of you.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Children">
      <p>
        ZhouYi Master AI is not directed at children under 13, and we do not
        knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child
        has sent personal information through the app, email{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="text-fg hover:underline">
          {CONTACT_EMAIL}
        </a>{" "}
        and we will delete it.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Data retention">
      <p>
        On-device data lives until you delete it in the app or delete the app.
        Your credit balance and reply records are kept on our server while the
        service runs, so your balance and subscription keep working. Email us to
        request their deletion.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Your rights">
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct,
        delete, or restrict processing of your personal data, and to lodge a
        complaint with a data protection authority. Email{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="text-fg hover:underline">
          {CONTACT_EMAIL}
        </a>{" "}
        and we'll respond within a reasonable time.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Changes to this policy">
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We'll change the
        effective date above and, for material changes, surface a notice in the
        app.
      </p>
    </DocSection>

    <DocSection title="Contact">
      <p>
        Questions about this policy?{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="text-fg hover:underline">
          {CONTACT_EMAIL}
        </a>
      </p>
    </DocSection>
  </article>
</Base>
